# Accepted vulnerabilities, one CVE id per line with a comment saying
# why and when to revisit. Use this when the PR gate flags a fixable
# HIGH/CRITICAL that only the upstream image maintainer can fix (the
# fix exists in a package, but the app has not shipped a rebuild yet).
# Trivy reads this file automatically.
#
# Example:
#   CVE-2026-9675  # seerr bundles old undici; drop when seerr ships a fix

# Not applicable: heap overflow on 32-bit platforms only (needs a >1 GB
# X.509 cert). The cluster runs 64-bit (amd64). openssl in the grafana
# kubectl toolbox image.
CVE-2026-31789

# Not applicable: handlebars RCE via crafted AST in compile(). In seerr,
# handlebars is an unused optional peer dependency of @ladjs/consolidate
# (via email-templates); all templates are pug and consolidate loads
# engines by file extension, so Handlebars.compile() is never reached.
# Maintainers confirmed and declined the pin:
# https://github.com/seerr-team/seerr/pull/3444
CVE-2026-33937

# Not reachable: Go crypto/tls skips cert re-validation on session
# resumption only when Config CAs are mutated between handshakes. The
# grafana kubectl toolbox runs kubectl as a short-lived client with one
# config per invocation, so that path never executes. Drop when
# helm-chart-toolbox-kubectl rebuilds with Go >= 1.24.13.
CVE-2025-68121

# Not reachable: node-tar gzip-bomb DoS needs the app to extract an
# attacker-supplied archive. Two hits are npm's vendored tar, which only
# runs at npm install time; seerr and velero-ui do not extract untrusted
# archives at runtime. Drop when they rebuild with tar >= 7.5.19.
CVE-2026-59873

# Waiting on rebuilds: golang.org/x/crypto/ssh fix is 0.55.0, and every
# Go image that bundles 0.53/0.54 flags it (grafana toolbox, alloy
# operator, node-exporter, kube-state-metrics). None of them run ssh.
# Drop when the monitoring images rebuild with x/crypto >= 0.55.
CVE-2026-56854
